WormWars — third-party data notice
==================================

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the code and documentation in this
repository. It does NOT cover the C. elegans connectome data that the code
depends on.

The connectome is published in:

    Cook SJ, Jarrell TA, Brittin CA, Wang Y, Bloniarz AE, Yakovlev MA,
    Nguyen KCQ, Tang LT-H, Bayer EA, Duerr JS, Bülow HE, Hobert O, Hall DH,
    Emmons SW (2019). Whole-animal connectomes of both Caenorhabditis elegans
    sexes. Nature 571:63-71. doi:10.1038/s41586-019-1352-7

and is distributed as supplementary data by wormwiring.org, which carries the
notice "Emmons Lab Copyright (c) 2020" and states no licence granting
redistribution. The Nature article is not open access.

For that reason NO connectome file is included in this repository: neither the
source spreadsheet nor the derived cache. Both are listed in .gitignore.

To obtain the data, run:

    python scripts/fetch_connectome.py

which downloads it from the original source and verifies its sha256 against the
value recorded in PROVENANCE.md. If the data is missing, the loader fails with
a clear message and offers no fallback and no synthetic substitute.

See PROVENANCE.md for the full chain: source URLs, hashes, the exact quantity
used, and every transformation applied.
